      "content": "Charles Howard Corgan (December 4, 1902 in Wagoner, Oklahoma – June 13, 1928), played professional baseball and football. In baseball, he played the infield for the Brooklyn Robins during the 1925 and 1927 seasons. He also played football for the Kansas City Blues/Cowboys, Hartford Blues and New York Giants from 1924 to 1927. He attended college at the University of Arkansas. He died from cancer in 1928.",
